WEBVTT

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.089
<v Callum Reid>Morning, everyone. Monday the thirteenth. You all hearing me?</v>

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.759
<v David Whitfield>Yep. Bit tinny, but that's probably this headset.</v>

00:00:15.199 --> 00:00:16.949
<v Olumide Adeyemi>You're coming through fine here.</v>

00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:20.030
<v Callum Reid>Right, lovely. Everyone survived the weekend, then?</v>

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:24.989
<v Marcus Hale>More importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office. Proper big one.</v>

00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:27.690
<v Sarah Okafor>Whose birthday?</v>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.490
<v Marcus Hale>Didn't get that far. Saw the cake, thought you'd want the important information.</v>

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:36.939
<v Hannah Price>Excellent investigation, that.</v>

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.119
<v Priya Raman>Has it actually got a name on it?</v>

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.350
<v Marcus Hale>Probably under the bit that's missing.</v>

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:50.460
<v Callum Reid>Right, before this becomes cake forensics, Jamie Brennan's absent today. We've got everyone else on.</v>

00:00:51.979 --> 00:00:54.079
<v Hannah Price>Yeah. Shall I start with mine?</v>

00:00:56.299 --> 00:01:03.299
<v Hannah Price>The near-miss write-up — I've had a first look, nothing major so far. Only at the initial notes stage, though.</v>

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.950
<v Callum Reid>Okay, cheers.</v>

00:01:07.349 --> 00:01:14.349
<v David Whitfield>Hannah asked me to pass on the pressure-drop investigation. That's cancelled our end; the supplier's doing it under warranty instead.</v>

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.739
<v Callum Reid>Fair enough, makes sense.</v>

00:01:19.469 --> 00:01:26.819
<v Hannah Price>And recalibrating the sensors on the heater box on one has moved to next week. That's the new deadline for mine.</v>

00:01:27.849 --> 00:01:29.049
<v Callum Reid>Yep, understood.</v>

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:40.010
<v Sarah Okafor>Pricey asked me to mention the filter swap on CT1 as well. She's had a first look, nothing major so far, but hasn't got as far as the swap yet.</v>

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:41.620
<v David Whitfield>Mm, okay.</v>

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.030
<v Sarah Okafor>And I already swapped the filter on the chiller on three yesterday. That one's sorted.</v>

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.159
<v David Whitfield>Ah, good. Lovely when they actually come out without a fight.</v>

00:01:56.069 --> 00:02:02.019
<v Marcus Hale>On my training records for the new starters, I've done the prep. Just the write-up left now.</v>

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.609
<v Callum Reid>Thanks. Um, one handover from me as well.</v>

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:13.889
<v Callum Reid>Organising the toolbox talk for the team — I'm handing that over to Olumide Adeyemi. Can you take that from me?</v>

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.199
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll take over organising the toolbox talk.</v>

00:02:18.689 --> 00:02:21.840
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. Right, today's new bits. What's happening on two?</v>

00:02:23.699 --> 00:02:28.250
<v Sarah Okafor>The line 2 robot's jammed. Production's held up on that at the minute.</v>

00:02:28.669 --> 00:02:32.870
<v Callum Reid>Is it just the jam, or are the sensors involved as well?</v>

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:41.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Can't call the sensors good yet. It needs clearing and those checking, not just pulling the jam out and assuming.</v>

00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:46.310
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, a clear gap isn't necessarily a happy sensor.</v>

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:56.530
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the line 2 robot by tomorrow morning. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.460
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, Saz. That's yours, then.</v>

00:03:00.189 --> 00:03:01.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, I'll take it.</v>

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:08.060
<v Callum Reid>Mide, can you take vibration readings on the hot bearing by Monday? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.080
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll take the vibration readings on the hot bearing.</v>

00:03:12.979 --> 00:03:17.879
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Monday as in today, yeah? Just checking, not trying to buy myself a week.</v>

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.439
<v Callum Reid>Today, yes. Definitely not next Monday.</v>

00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:23.719
<v David Whitfield>Worth a try, though.</v>

00:03:25.689 --> 00:03:29.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Ha. No, understood — that one takes priority for me.</v>

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.270
<v Priya Raman>And I'll run the monthly fire alarm test on Friday.</v>

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:35.300
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, Pri. Agreed.</v>

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:40.659
<v Marcus Hale>Friday's getting a theme. Isn't that cake day as well?</v>

00:03:41.509 --> 00:03:46.409
<v Priya Raman>The charity bake sale on Friday, yeah. Nothing engineering-related about that, before anyone starts.</v>

00:03:47.189 --> 00:03:49.289
<v Hannah Price>Depends how your sponge turns out.</v>

00:03:49.949 --> 00:03:51.349
<v Priya Raman>Oi. Structurally sound, mine.</v>

00:03:53.139 --> 00:03:55.939
<v Callum Reid>All right, any other observations before we finish?</v>

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:03.530
<v Marcus Hale>Only that I heard a slight rattle from the Atlas. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.909
<v Callum Reid>Okay, noted. No action off that.</v>

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:13.500
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, did I clip out halfway through? Teams went a bit funny.</v>

00:04:14.169 --> 00:04:17.670
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, we got you. Your picture froze, voice was fine.</v>

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:21.610
<v Marcus Hale>Probably an improvement, the frozen picture.</v>

00:04:23.079 --> 00:04:24.480
<v Sarah Okafor>Wouldn't like to comment.</v>

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.629
<v Callum Reid>Very diplomatic. Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.509
<v Priya Raman>Cheers, all.</v>

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.360
<v David Whitfield>Cheers.</v>
